# Sample Recipe

File: opm/examples/recipe.oot

A recipe is a key=value manifest for offline key resolution. It maps package names to local tarball paths.

```
[recipe]
hello-world = ./pkgs/hello-world-1.2.3.tar.gz
json-parser = ./pkgs/json-parser-2.1.0.tar.gz
http-client = ./pkgs/http-client-1.5.4.tar.gz
```

## Usage

`ooda opm add hello-world` resolves via the recipe first, then via the catalog. Fail-closed if neither has it.
